      en: "Tahiti Lagoonarium is located on the west coast of Tahiti near Punaauia, a natural aquarium in a protected lagoon. It hosts a variety of marine life including tropical fish, rays, and small sharks. The lagoon covers about 3 hectares and reaches depths of 4 meters. Visitors can snorkel and explore colorful coral reefs. The facility opened in 2007 and offers guided tours. The Lagoonarium is part of a larger protected area safeguarding coastal ecosystems. Water temperature ranges between 27-30°C. It is popular with tourists seeking easy access to marine life. The facility collaborates with marine biologists to monitor biodiversity.",
